{
 "_comment": [
  "THE trigger-compatibility table. A wish built on a real game item (base_item) must ride WITH that item's own action, never instead of it (docs/ITEM_TRIGGERS_PLAN.md §3).",
  "One table, three readers: make_item (ItemTriggers.java), E1 (tools/parts-coverage.py) and the tests. Edit it here and every reader moves together; no reader keeps a copy.",
  "alsoRides (optional): other shapes that ride the same action, offered in the guidance beside the redirect (a bow's wish is `arrow` where it lands, or `on_shot` the moment he shoots).",
  "actions: what the base does on right-click in vanilla, the items that do it, and `redirect` — the shape a wish that would take the click must use instead (null = no trigger rides this action; the wish is a property, or needs another base).",
  "takesTheClick: shapes that run the wish on right-click, so they conflict with any base that has a use action of its own.",
  "neverOnARealBase: shapes that never run on a real base at all (VanillaCarrierAbilities only drives them on our own item) — refused with the alternative (decided in F.0; the plan's other option, wiring them, is not taken: nothing in the corpus needs it).",
  "needsAction: shapes that only exist on bases with one of these actions (an arrow needs something that shoots).",
  "suffixes: a base not listed by name takes the action of the first suffix it ends with. A named item always wins (milk_bucket is drink, not bucket).",
  "A base with no entry has action `none`: nothing of its own happens on right-click in the air, so a wish may take the click. Tools that act only on a BLOCK (a hoe tilling, a shovel pathing) and block items (a torch placing) are deliberately `none`: the child asked for a wand made of it, and the corpus audit (§6 group D) agrees."
 ],
